#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151961 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152170 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb49535-c9cc-5d5a-9fd0-a6fd7e5df3bf" :knowledge-point/title "The Division Algorithm For Positive Integers"}] :question/id #uuid "909d813e-aab7-5e84-be60-2434383064a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-6499" :question/problem "Let $a=85$ and $n=8$. Find positive integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a = qn+r$, where $0 \\leq r < n$, and determine $q \\cdot r$." :question/worked-solution "Dividing $85$ by $8$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{10}} < 85\\div 8 < 11\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So\n\n$$\nq={\\color{red}{10}}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r = a-qn$. This gives\n\n$$\nr = 85 - (10)(8) = {\\color{blue}{5}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n85 = qn + r\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n85 = 10_(⏟)_(q) \\cdot 8 + 5_(⏟)_(r)\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nq \\cdot r = 10 \\cdot 5 = 50\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151962 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "374cafa1-c178-5125-bda0-19b4e1c51892" :knowledge-point/title "The Division Algorithm For Negative Integers"}] :question/id #uuid "58d4cedc-5fb8-5592-a75d-687a0c67da21" :question/math-academy-id "e-6500" :question/problem "Let $a=-44$ and $n=6$. Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a = qn+r$, where $0 \\leq r < n$, and determine $q\\cdot r$." :question/worked-solution "Dividing $-44$ by $6$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{-8}} < -44\\div 6 < -7\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So\n\n$$\nq={\\color{red}{-8}}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by solving $r = a-qn$. This gives\n\n$$\nr = -44 - (-8)(6) = {\\color{blue}{4}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n-44 = qn + r\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n-44 = (-8)_(⏟)_(q) \\cdot 6 + 4_(⏟)_(r)\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nq\\cdot r = -8 \\cdot 4 = -32\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152766 :